Stuff I haven't seen suggested yet:

- Consider wearing studded leather armor.  In fact, pick up any studded
  leather you find that you can determine to be non-cursed (your pet will
  pick it up or at least happily step on it).  Comparison shop.  You'd be
  surprised how easy it is to find enchanted studded leather.  Even leather
  armor can be a boon.  Neither interferes with spellcasting.
- Arguably, you could just wear the mithril, and concentrate on training
  your dagger skill up, since you won't be able to cast spells very much in
  the early game anyway.  Personally though, I like training up spells
  whenever possible, and taking off armor to do it would be an
  inconvenience.  Just an option.
- My rule of thumb is to never enter the Mines until I have at least 50 hp.
  I do this even for combat-ready barbarians, so it goes double for
  wizards.
- Clear every level before going down, and go down as soon as it's clear.
  Don't bother dawdling.
- The protection racket refers to a strategy for improving your intrinsic
  AC.  As you probably know, you can improve it to 1 by donating to a
  priest; the racket allows you to gather enough money to do so, fairly
  early.  It can be fun, but a bit risky, as it requires going into the
  Mines while you're still low level.

